  "period_note": "Year-end position from the Annual Report's own multi-year 'Key operating and financial data' summary table (audited), cross-validated against the Balance Sheet wherever available. This bank has operated with deeply negative shareholders' equity and a deeply negative Capital Adequacy Ratio (CAR) throughout the entire researched period (2013-2024), i.e. it has been technically insolvent by conventional accounting/regulatory measures for over a decade — a legacy of the 2006 collapse and nationalization of its predecessor, The Oriental Bank Limited, on fraud/mismanagement grounds. As a Shariah-based Islamic bank, reports 'Investment' rather than conventional 'Loans and Advances', and 'Classified Investments' rather than 'NPL'. This year's own annual report PDF is not in the local archive; all FY2019 figures independently cross-validated across the FY2020, FY2021, and FY2022 reports' comparative columns, which are mutually consistent.",
